id: pm-web-lgg5
title: Show real paginated item history and live updates
description: "Verify and fix the compact-default history mismatch. Request an explicit supported projection through the authorized project runner; normalize documented oldest-first API pages with newest-first panel rendering; bound reads and expose has_more and a cursor; preserve membership checks. Acceptance: SDK-created non-git tracker route regression with at least three mutations and a terminal close; behavioral revert failure proof; real npm CLI output from 2026.10.20, 2026.10.27 and 2026.10.28 through the normalizer; browser detail and live-copy checks with screenshots; typed errors and remedies; README API documentation; pm-changelog entry; targeted tests, typecheck and lint locally; full npm and Bun CI release gates with counts. No deployment, merge or release."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[2]: "gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1617","gh:unbraind/pm-web#274"
created_at: "2026-10-28T15:59:19.401Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T18:56:33.840Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-29T18:56:33.337Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-29T18:56:33.337Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Explicit supported history projection through authorized project runner; oldest_first API ordering honors upstream order or absent-as-oldest; bounded pages with has_more and cursor; newest-first detail panel and live refresh; SDK-created non-git HTTP regression with three mutations plus close and behavioral revert proof; actual npm output from 2026.10.20 2026.10.27 and 2026.10.28 normalized in tests; real browser screenshot and live-copy proof; typed refusals with remedies; README API docs and generated changelog; targeted local tests typecheck lint and full npm plus Bun CI gate evidence
release: 2026.10.29
comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T16:00:16.203Z",codex-agent,"Verification found an important distinction: projectPm dispatches native history in-process through PmClient.run, rather than the CLI default-selection layer. On the pinned SDK 2026.10.20, an SDK-created non-git tracker with create and two updates returned history with three entries by default; explicit compact returned compact_history. Continuing with the actual HTTP route and requested npm releases before deciding whether the suspected empty-panel defect reproduces. No application code changed."
  "2026-10-28T16:05:55.123Z",codex-agent,"REPRODUCED with npm pm 2026.10.28 injected only into module resolution for the unchanged HTTP route: HTTP 200, compact_history=4, history absent, order=newest_first, operations close/update/update/create, and UI fallback history length=0. The fixture was SDK-created outside git with create, two updates and close. npm 2026.10.20 and 2026.10.27 SDK dispatch returned 4 full rows, while their CLI defaults returned compact rows. Pinned dependency remains unchanged. The test database is unavailable, so route verification uses the repository authorization-query stub pattern with real authenticated HTTP and real SDK trackers; no hosted services or Docker are accessed. Design: explicit compact summary projection (the panel uses operation/time, never patches), normalized oldest-first API rows, fixed page size and opaque backwards cursor, newest-first panel plus load older, and live refresh resets to the latest page. The native history query supports latest-entry limit but no backwards cursor, so older API pages will request only the needed bounded latest suffix and trim it before responding."
  "2026-10-28T16:17:51.083Z",codex-agent,"Targeted verification passed 5/5 tests (0 skipped), including nine actual npm CLI output cases: default, full and compact with limit 3 on each of 2026.10.20, 2026.10.27 and 2026.10.28. Current default was newest_first and lacked history; all normalized timelines ended in close. A 56-entry real timeline returned exactly 50 patch-free API rows below 25000 response characters; authenticated non-member reads stayed 404 and anonymous reads 401. Revert proof in a disposable source copy: restoring only src/routes/pm.ts to origin/main made the focused route regression fail (exit 1); fixed worktree unchanged. Read-cost limitation: the supported HistoryCommandOptions declaration has limit but no reverse cursor, and open upstream search found no exact reverse-history cursor issue. Backwards API pages use physical-index boundaries and bounded response projection, re-reading the needed native suffix. No upstream issue was filed."
  "2026-10-28T16:22:04.096Z",codex-agent,"Browser verification passed at 1440 and 390 pixels using the existing Playwright/ephemeral-server harness and real authorized history routes over a real non-git SDK tracker. Both views rendered 50 newest rows, paged back through create with no duplicates, displayed real dates and operations, refreshed a new committed update through live-copy, reset the older-page cursor and had no horizontal overflow or page errors. Screenshots: artifacts/item-history/item-history-1440.png and artifacts/item-history/item-history-390.png (ignored binary evidence). Final behavioral revert proof: route-only origin/main reversion in a disposable copy failed because actual panel actions were four undefined values instead of create/update/update/close; fixed focused regression passed 1/1 after the revert run. Local build, test typecheck, server/frontend typecheck, lint, full docstring gate and zero-duplication gate passed. The pinned changelog generator selects only closed items; closing this item is forbidden, so generate a pending changelog fragment and retain canonical regeneration for orchestrator verification. Canonical CHANGELOG entry remains an explicit acceptance gap until that step."
  "2026-10-28T16:23:42.269Z",codex-agent,Upstream ordering behavior referenced by this task is unbraind/pm-cli#1617; this package normalizes it and does not change or file upstream issues. Backwards native cursor performance is tracked separately by pm-web-f3xo.
  "2026-10-28T16:29:52.424Z",codex-agent,"Draft PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/274 . Initial CI run: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/40726225806 (initial head; final evidence commit will require a new exact-head run). The pm-linked command passed all 4 real route/normalizer regressions but its first fresh npm installation timed out; the compatibility test now preserves noncredential networking configuration while removing credential variables and forcing the public npm registry plus credential-free user config. Retrying the pm-linked command with already-installed exact versions and verifying fresh npm installs separately. Existing live-copy unit tests passed 6/6. The generated pending changelog fragment is linked; canonical generation/check passed unchanged because this item is intentionally unclosed."
  "2026-10-28T16:34:06.809Z",codex-agent,"Final local evidence: pm test --run --progress --shared-host-safe passed 1/1 linked commands containing 5/5 tests and all nine real CLI projections (0 failures/skips). A separate fresh-install compatibility rerun passed 1/1 with nine outputs after the networking-environment correction. The fixed real HTTP route was also re-run with npm SDK 2026.10.28: HTTP 200, history=4, oldest_first, actions create/update/update/close, has_more=false and null cursor. Existing live-copy tests passed 6/6; build:test and lint passed after the compatibility-test edit. Full npm/Bun release gates remain CI-only, with initial CI still queued. The current-head checks are always available at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/274/checks . Draft remains required for the canonical changelog-entry criterion: generator selects only closed items and closure is reserved for the orchestrator. Pending entry is generated and linked; no thresholds, dependency pins, hosted services or release policy were changed. Stop waiting for CI at the queue-rules 30-minute cutoff and report any still-pending counts honestly."
  "2026-10-28T16:37:47.248Z",codex-agent,"Final review found an additional real cursor race: enough writes between the head probe and suffix read can remove the requested boundary from that suffix. Treat this as typed history_cursor_stale with restart guidance, rather than letting a missing boundary reach hashing and surface as generic unavailability. Adding a deterministic real-SDK concurrent-append regression before the final CI wait."
  "2026-10-28T16:40:42.986Z",codex-agent,"The additional cursor-race regression passed 1/1 with real SDK reads and five writes deliberately admitted between the head and suffix reads. Restoring only the pre-fix history-page function in a disposable copy failed that same test with ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE from hashing an absent boundary (exit 1), proving the new stale-cursor branch. The implementation now returns typed 409 history_cursor_stale with restart guidance for that race. Build:server, build:test and lint passed after this change. Superseded CI runs are being cancelled to reserve runner time for the final head; their incomplete gates are not counted as evidence."
  "2026-10-28T16:42:43.738Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted rerun after the cursor-race fix: pm test --run --progress --shared-host-safe passed 1/1 linked commands, 5/5 tests, nine real npm projections, 0 failures and 0 skips. Cursor-race focused proof also passed 1/1 and failed on behavioral revert. Superseded CI runs 40726225806 and 40727488127 were cancelled; neither supplies final-head gate evidence. Final-head npm/Bun CI remains the pending full-gate requirement, visible through PR 274 checks. The canonical changelog entry also remains pending orchestrator closure; generated pending entry is preserved. Claim released for review; item intentionally not closed."
  "2026-10-28T16:55:20.421Z",codex-agent,"Final-head CI Node 26 reported 850/852 tests passing, with two actionable regressions: the managed extension installation resolves host pm 2026.10.23 despite the source pin, so the compatibility test must install the exact requested 2026.10.20 rather than assume the local host matches it; and an existing real HTTP lifecycle test requires recorded history messages. Preserve those messages with an explicit full history projection plus its same-snapshot diff indices, then bound and sanitize the browser rows. Adding real full/diff output cases for all requested npm versions and a route assertion preserving the update message. Coverage measured 92.42 percent lines/statements, 84.79 branches and 96.21 functions before the failed test exit; this is a failing run, not a full-gate pass. Run: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/40728719161 ."
  "2026-10-28T16:58:41.470Z",codex-agent,"CI findings corrected locally: the real recorded update message is preserved by explicit --full --diff --limit reads, with same-snapshot diff indices used for paging; messages are bounded to 512 characters and raw patches/diff values are omitted. The compatibility test now checks the actual local package version and installs every requested version that differs, including 2026.10.20 when the CI host is 2026.10.23. Final targeted pm run passed 5/5 tests and 12 actual CLI outputs across all three requested releases, with 0 skipped. Build, all typechecks, lint, docstrings and zero duplication passed. CI run 40728719161 is a failed prior implementation (Node 26: 850/852 tests, 2 failures; Bun skipped), never acceptance evidence. The 30-minute CI waiting cutoff has now elapsed; push the corrections and report the new exact-head run as pending rather than claiming full gates passed."
  "2026-10-28T17:01:31.540Z",codex-agent,"Clarification to the earlier CI-host inference: current main package metadata now pins pm 2026.10.23, verified directly from the repository. CI tests the PR merge tree, so the observed newer host follows the updated base; it is not evidence that managed extension installation changed the root pin. This branch does not change dependency pins. The compatibility test now works against either local host by installing exact requested versions whenever needed. The final full/diff implementation passed browser verification again at 1440 and 390 pixels, with the same two screenshot paths and live-copy/pagination assertions."
  "2026-10-28T17:02:13.291Z",codex-agent,"Final message-preservation revert proof: restoring only the pre-correction history service functions in a disposable copy made the real route test fail because the recorded exercise update flags message was undefined (exit 1). The fixed focused route test passed 1/1 immediately afterward. Full/diff mode also passed all 5 linked tests, all 12 npm output cases and the two refreshed browser screenshots; pending full gates and the canonical changelog entry remain explicit draft blockers. No item was closed and the claim is released."
  "2026-10-28T17:05:11.040Z",codex-agent,"CI cutoff handoff: corrected source commit 39258af is queued in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/40731985115 . Verified full release-gate count for the corrected implementation is 0/4; npm and Bun on Node 22 and 26 are pending, not passed. The previous run 40728719161 failed 850/852 tests on each Node version with the two now-corrected regressions; Bun was skipped. Local corrected evidence remains 5/5 linked tests, 12 real CLI cases, 6/6 live-copy tests, 2 browser widths, passing build/typecheck/lint/docstrings/duplication/changelog checks, and behavioral revert failures. This final tracker-only handoff will trigger another exact-head CI run; PR 274 checks and the PR body identify that latest run. No further CI waiting after the established cutoff. Canonical changelog entry awaits orchestrator closure; generated pending entry is preserved. Item and follow-up stay unclosed; agent claim is released."
  "2026-10-28T19:01:57.080Z",codex-agent,"Resumed per orchestrator: previous final-head npm/Bun CI passed, but CodeQL reported a new high CSRF finding in test/helpers/item-history-harness.ts. Replace the bare Express/cookie harness with createApp so the production session and CSRF boundary applies. Audit sibling test helpers for this pattern, add cookie-authenticated rejection and legitimate token-bootstrap controls, merge current origin/main with a two-parent merge, run focused history/live-copy/browser and typecheck/lint, then wait up to 45 minutes for fresh CI and CodeQL. No alert dismissal or suppression. Sub-agent delegation is prohibited by the task rules, so security-boundary investigation and candidate review are separate local passes."
  "2026-10-28T19:14:07.718Z",codex-agent,"Security-boundary and candidate-review passes completed without delegation. The affected path was the bare cookie parser in itemHistoryHarness feeding real mutating pm routes without the production CSRF guard. The helper now creates the production app; browser callers no longer add replacement API/static handlers. All sibling test helpers were checked: pg-harness already uses createApp; the cookie-based unit fixtures in sw-idempotency-http, rate-limit and pure-units already mount csrfProtection before handlers, so no second instance in this PR scope remained. Local ordered verification passed build:test, 11/11 focused history/CSRF/live-copy tests, typecheck, lint, docstrings (885 documented declarations), duplication (0 clones), and browser checks at 1440/390 with real account bootstrap and unchanged screenshot paths. Four malicious cookie request classes return 403 without changing tracker history; a cookie/header token obtained from GET /api/auth/me permits the real comment with 201. Behavioral revert in a disposable source copy: restoring only the old helper made the new test fail on 201 versus expected 403 (exit 1); fixed focused control passed 1/1 afterward. No production security middleware, alert metadata, suppression or authentication rule was weakened. Main merged cleanly with its dependency/changelog changes; merge commit will have both parents. Fresh npm/Bun and CodeQL evidence will be required on the resulting head; wait budget is now 45 minutes per orchestrator."
  "2026-10-28T20:13:15.238Z",codex-agent,"Re-review resumed. Rule: pagination success must prove complete coverage from the same read snapshot; a head probe is only a sizing hint, never evidence of suffix completeness. Main is already an ancestor after fetch, so no new merge is needed. Investigating every package history reader, runner output path, cursor consumer and packed consumer. Add adversarial real non-git append schedules, reject incomplete suffixes with typed restart guidance, and preserve existing tests. The instruction names one blocker; non-blocking findings were requested because no additional review findings are published on GitHub."
  "2026-10-28T20:17:37.232Z",codex-agent,"Class audit completed: src/services/item-history.ts is the sole head-probe/latest-suffix paginator. Its success path now verifies the entire expected contiguous physical interval in the same suffix that validates the anchor, so partial and empty older pages cannot certify exhaustion. Audit covered routes, the PmClient dispatcher and subprocess JSON parser in pm-runner, SDK resume packets and mutation replay, CLI command registration and its JSON/human output, and npm/Bun packed acceptance. Sibling readers use SDK forward cursors or authoritative complete reads rather than separately sized suffixes; there is no separate pm-web history CLI/TOON paginator. The common service protects all hosts/backends and compiled dist bytes were regenerated. Adversarial source and compiled-module tests passed 60 real non-git schedules (three limits, five append counts, two read interleavings), checking exact coverage and restart traversal to entry one. Source-only behavioral revert in a disposable copy failed on the first six-entry, limit-two, two-append case: missing expected typed refusal (exit 1). No existing test was removed or weakened. README now documents the concurrent-suffix restart case."
  "2026-10-28T20:20:50.973Z",codex-agent,"Final local re-review evidence: 13/13 focused tests passed (history, live-copy and twelve real npm CLI output shapes on 2026.10.20, 2026.10.27 and 2026.10.28), zero failures/skips. The PM-linked history/live-copy command then passed 12/12 after both disposable behavioral revert checks. Compiled-only revert also failed with missing expected rejection; source fixed control and compiled fixed control both pass. Browser passed at 1440/390 with two regenerated screenshots at artifacts/item-history/item-history-1440.png and artifacts/item-history/item-history-390.png, 50 newest rows, older traversal, live refresh, zero duplicate rows and no horizontal overflow. Build:test, server/frontend typecheck, lint, 885 documented declarations and zero duplication passed. Sequential isolated-home npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed static/build stages then refused at PostgreSQL preflight because the local test database is unavailable; no tests were skipped and these are not full-gate passes. Fresh CI supplies the required full npm/Bun counts on the new head. Current main is already merged; no rebase, force push or new dependency bump. PR is draft until fresh gates and CodeQL pass. Only the one concrete finding supplied in this re-review is available; no further non-blocking findings are published on GitHub. Claim will be released before push; final CI receipts will be in PR 274 and its checks so the tested commit stays unchanged."
